 "instruction": "The `shell` tool in `sanctuary/tools/builtin.py` runs every command with `shell=True`, so one command string can chain, pipe or substitute (`foo; rm -rf ~`). Make it safe by default:\n\n- By default, tokenize the command POSIX-style (`shlex`) and run it without a shell. Then `;`, `|`, `&&` and `$(...)` are inert, and extra tokens reach the program as literal arguments.\n- Full shell interpretation stays available through an explicit `use_shell: true` parameter.\n- A command that can't be tokenized (unbalanced quotes) returns a failed `ToolResult` whose error says the command couldn't be parsed, instead of raising. An empty command still fails with \"No command provided\".\n- Update the tool's registered description and parameters (in `create_default_registry`) to document `use_shell`.\n\nAlso harden the `run_code` Docker sandbox: add `--pids-limit=256`, `--cap-drop=ALL` and `--security-opt=no-new-privileges` to the `docker run` arguments.",
